@page "/wiki/species-traits"
@page "/wiki/species-traits/{Key}"

@*
    What a founding species can be given, and what it costs to give.

    Three hundred and sixty-four of them, and the reader's question is nearly always a budget one:
    what can be had for two points, and which of these hand points back. So the cost is a column and
    a heading rather than a line of prose inside the card.

    A trait states its restrictions as flat lists rather than as conditions - there is no requirement
    tree on one anywhere - so the requirement columns stay empty and what it may be taken with is
    said as facts instead.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Species Traits - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.SpeciesTraits" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it named one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
